From 38e85bba773240dc9b94b1bf1007c186f4aa59bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 06:30:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 17/28] test: declare the abc and chronik tests' parameters as
 class attributes

New contrib/devtools/declarative-test-params.py rewrites a test's
set_test_params() as class attributes when the method only assigns
values to self.<name>. A value may refer to parameters assigned before
it, e.g. `[[...]] * self.num_nodes` becomes `[[...]] * num_nodes`.
Comments are kept. Methods that compute anything else (use self.options,
call functions other than list()/range() and the like, have control
flow) are left alone and reported.

Applied to the abc* and chronik_* tests: 105 of 109 converted. The four
left need runtime values or calls. Every converted module imports, and
the full functional suite gives the same per-test results as before.
The one difference in a run was an RPC timeout under load in
feature_reindex.py, which this commit does not touch and which passes on
its own.
